Help me plan a FoundryVTT orchestration system and control panel website called Hivemind.

# Hivemind
Hivemind would serve as a self-hosted deployable setup for managing many FoundryVTT instances for personal use.

## Defintions:
        Foundry Instance -> A discreet container running FoundryVTT
        Foundry World -> A FoundryVTT world containing scenes, actors, chat, and other VTT content
        Active World -> A running Foundry Instance
        Front Page -> An authenticated webpage that players, GMs, and admins can use to connect to and manage games
        Orchestrator -> A backend container that handles all API calls to manage the
## Ideas:
        The orchestrator would run in a docker container
        The orchestrator  would be tasked with spinning up and down containers running the Docker image of FoundryVTT.
        Each world would run in a dedicated instance
        Each world would have a pre-made admin user
        The GM of each world could be assigned from the admin panel by the Admin
        The panel would contain a package manager that allows for per-instance Foundry module management by the GM or admin
        There would be an import feature to bring in worlds from outside the system
        Each Foundry instance would have its own per-player assets
        All modules would be downloaded to a single source directory and symbolically linked to all instances that require it (prevent duplication)
        All world and instance configuration would be instance specific
        There would be the ability for the admin to create a template world which a new instance could be created with
        By default, when an instance starts it starts with its own world
        Hivemind would have a login system which would allow SSO for all instances, skipping the join page
        To skip the join page, there would be a loading page for a starting container which would hide the startup and auto-login
        The login would use a custom per-user key which would be used as the Foundry Instance's password.
        The Foundry instance would login the user automatically if their cookies contain the appropriate per-user key
        The per-user key would be assigned at login by Hivemind's authentication system
        The authentication system would allow passwords, Passkeys (one click login w/ Password Manager), and Social Login (Google, Apple, etc.)
        The front page would show all worlds on the majority of the screen
        The front page would show all active worlds on a quickly accessible panel
        All Foundry Instances will be status pinged by the Orchestrator to find the number of active users and active status
        All Foundry Instances with no players active for a configurable amount of time will be shutdown by the orchestrator
        The front page would have a button to (shutdown and restart when in active status) or (start when in off status)
        The orchestrator should track the status of each instance as active, idle, or disabled
        Active status indicates an instance is turned on, Idle status indicates the instance is shutdown, Disabled means the instance cannot be turned on except by the admin or GM
        The front page and the orchestrator would communicate exclusively through the API
        The API would require authentication for all requests
        The front page would require login for all requests
        Any traffic connecting to any page on the front page (including specific Foundry Instances) would require authentication
        Any non-authenticated traffic would be redirected to the authentication
        Any traffic redirected to authentication would be redirected back to their original destination
        Each instance contains a list of all users with their authenticated tokens stored as passwords
        The orchestrator enforces access and visibility for worlds per-player, preventing users who are not players from seeing or connecting to games
        A player can be assigned as a GM by an Admin
        Each GM can have a custom homepage which they can customize with a background, colors, etc.
